# reflows, never anything that changed a word. Wire it up once per clone with
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# and `git blame` skips to the commit that last touched the content. A SHA here
# that no longer exists is silently ignored rather than reported, so an entry
# only earns its place after the commit it names is settled.

